# Render

Render (https://render.com) is a cloud application platform for deploying, securing, and scaling applications, from hundred-line prototypes to complex multi-service architectures.

## Start here

Route according to your task:

- To connect, install, set up, or configure Render for this agent environment, read https://render.com/agents.md and follow its steps in order. Treat it as a procedure, not as reference documentation.
- To perform a Render platform task (deploy a service, debug a failed deploy, add a database, configure a domain, scale a service, etc.), read https://render.com/agents/tasks.md.
- To retrieve documentation for a single topic, use the Documentation index below, search https://render.com/api/agent/docs-search?query={query}, or fetch the relevant page as Markdown from https://render.com/docs/{slug}.md.

## Agent interfaces

- Authenticated, account-scoped platform actions (Render MCP Server): https://mcp.render.com/mcp
- MCP server documentation: https://render.com/docs/mcp-server.md
- MCP OAuth 2.0 authorization server metadata: https://api.render.com/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
- Public documentation keyword search: https://render.com/api/agent/docs-search
- Public documentation retrieval as Markdown: https://render.com/docs/{slug}.md
- Render REST API documentation: https://render.com/docs/api.md
- Render REST API OpenAPI specification: https://api-docs.render.com/openapi/render-public-api-1.json
- Render REST API reference material: https://api-docs.render.com/llms.txt
- Render REST API authentication (API keys): https://render.com/docs/api.md#setup
- Render webhooks documentation: https://render.com/docs/webhooks.md
- Installable Render agent skills: https://render.com/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json

## Setup guides

Use the guide that matches this agent environment and follow it in order:

- Claude Desktop: https://render.com/agents/claude-desktop.md
- Claude Code: https://render.com/agents/claude.md
- Codex Desktop: https://render.com/agents/codex-desktop.md
- Codex CLI: https://render.com/agents/codex.md
- Cursor: https://render.com/agents/cursor.md
- OpenCode: https://render.com/agents/opencode.md
- Pi: https://render.com/agents/pi.md

## Documentation

For the complete documentation corpus, use https://render.com/llms-full.txt only when the task requires broad access to the full Render documentation set.

Do not fetch it for single-topic lookups (it is over 900 KB). Instead, fetch individual .md pages or use the search endpoint.

### Core Platform

#### Start

- [Your First Render Deploy](https://render.com/docs/your-first-deploy.md): Run your web app in minutes.
- [Deploy for Free](https://render.com/docs/free.md): Preview the Render platform with free web services and datastores.
- [Platform Features by Plan](https://render.com/docs/platform-features-by-plan.md): Enable powerful platform capabilities with a Pro, Scale, or Enterprise plan.
- [Using Render with Coding Agents](https://render.com/docs/llm-support.md): Deploy and manage apps using LLM-powered tools.
- [Render FAQ](https://render.com/docs/faq.md)

##### Migrate from…

- [Migrate from Heroku to Render](https://render.com/docs/migrate-from-heroku.md): Bring your Heroku apps and data to the Render platform.
- [Migrate from Railway to Render](https://render.com/docs/migrate-from-railway.md): Bring your Railway apps and data to the Render platform.

#### Compute

- [Render Compute Plans](https://render.com/docs/compute-plans.md): Specify your service's available CPU and RAM.

##### Service types

- [Services and Service Types](https://render.com/docs/service-types.md): Understand Render's core building blocks.
- [Static Sites](https://render.com/docs/static-sites.md): Host your website's frontend (React, Next.js, etc.) over a global CDN.
- [Web Services](https://render.com/docs/web-services.md): Host dynamic web apps (Express, Django, etc.) at a public URL.
- [Private Services](https://render.com/docs/private-services.md): Host apps that only accept traffic from your other services.
- [Background Workers](https://render.com/docs/background-workers.md): Offload asynchronous tasks to a separate service listening on a queue.
- [Cron Jobs](https://render.com/docs/cronjobs.md): Run periodic tasks on a schedule you define.
- [Multi-Service Architectures on Render](https://render.com/docs/multi-service-architecture.md)

##### Data storage

- [Render Key Value](https://render.com/docs/key-value.md): Provision Redis®-compatible datastores for caching and job queues.
- [Persistent Disks](https://render.com/docs/disks.md): Preserve your service's filesystem changes across deploys.

